select 've-front-of-house', 'vegans-explore', 'Logan', $pb$BUILD RECORD, 2026-10-31 (Logan). Everything built for BrandDesk so far, where it lives, what is live, and what comes next, so the work can be picked up from here with nothing pieced back together. Full detail: CLAUDE.md in lesaruss/vegansexplore-com, section "BrandDesk". Branch claude/gifted-cori-ummpqg (not merged to main: none of these pages are on vegansexplore.com until it is).

1. THE FRAME (the client website template). business/site.html at /business/sample/site: Green Leaf Kitchen's site drawn only from its Cartridge (business/sample/cartridge.js, window.VE_CARTRIDGE). Pages Home, Menu, Order, About, Visit; menu filtered by section; Square-style cart when ordering is connected; photo sets (Outside, At night, Inside, The team); map and hours; reversed logo in the footer; schema.org data. 24 menu and 7 space photos (Higgsfield, illustrative).
2. MAKE IT YOURS. The sample bar's Their brand / Island bright / Night lounge redraws the same site with only colors and type changed (LOOKS, applyLook).
3. THE BRAND KIT (intake and the owner's editor). /business/brand (business/brand.html), guided view. Editors for Logo, Colors (readability score, Lock refused under 3:1), Type, Voice, Story, Menu (Suggest via ve-brand-kit, Claude), Hours and details, Photos. Real kits stored per listing: /business/brand?listing=<slug>, tables ve_cartridges, ve_cartridge_people, ve_cartridge_edits; a super admin starts one (kit_create, filled from the listing).
4. MANAGED BY US and HAVE US DO IT. /business has a Managed by us tab (passport.html, BIZ.managed). The Restaurant Guide's audit has Or have us do it on every Fix. Both open /public/ve-managed.js, sent to ve-brand-kit managed_interest: a lead (initiative branddesk) shown in the Inbox as a Managed marketing request, an email to the team and a confirmation to them. Nothing charged.
5. THE AGREEMENT. /business/agreement, version 2026-10-31, approved by Sean ("I was able to review it, and I'm okay with the terms"). No liability or indemnity clause yet; add in a later version (a change is a new version, matched in ve-branddesk AGREEMENT_VERSION).
6. CHECKOUT AND STRIPE, LIVE since 2026-10-31. /business/managed?listing=<slug>: Your plan (setup at once, 3 x $500 or 6 x $250; social +$500), The agreement (name typed and ticked), Review and pay (Stripe Checkout). Edge function ve-branddesk. One subscription per client; setup installments dropped by a subscription schedule after 3 or 6 payments; Pause $99 a month, 1 to 3 months a year, not during installments; cancel (super admin) reports setup still owed. Live on the Vegans Explore Stripe key (ve_site_settings branddesk.live true). Checkout opens only for listings Sean opens (branddesk.allowed, empty today) and for super admins. Proven in test mode end to end; checked live with a real $1,500 session for Sobe Vegan, expired, row removed.
7. ONBOARDING, THE LIBRARY, THE ASSET SHEET. On payment: setup_paid_at when paid at once (installments: once their invoices reach 3 or 6); the website archive starts (every page up to 40 plus pictures, styles, fonts and scripts, links pointed at the copies, manifest.json and README.txt, one ZIP; proven on lovelifecafe.com: 15 pages, 40 files, opens offline); the onboarding checklist (welcome call within 2 days, confirmed owner, website archived, brand kit started, Google manager access, domain access, social access if bought, starter shoot booked, first files in the Library). Library: private bucket branddesk-library, table ve_branddesk_files; previews always, full-size downloads of what we make only once setup is paid in full; their archive and documents always theirs. The client sees Managed by us on their business dashboard (?tab=brand&pd=managed: Getting started, Your Library with Download everything as one ZIP that includes the asset sheet and the menu spreadsheet, Your asset sheet from their Cartridge with CSV and HTML downloads), drawn by /public/ve-branddesk-client.js. The sample business shows Green Leaf Kitchen's. Depot > BrandDesk (/admin/depot/branddesk): Clients, one client (signature, plan, End it, tick steps, Archive it now, Add to their Library) and Who can sign up.
8. PREVIEW. Depot > Preview journeys > BrandDesk walks every screen above without signing up or paying.

STILL OPEN. Merge the branch to main (on Sean's word). Not built: emailing a client when a file lands; the 30-day download window after an end; a Community Manager's view of their accounts; liability and indemnity in the agreement; the trademark check before the name BrandDesk goes public.

